# Testing Guidelines

## Testing Strategy

- Write tests before fixing bugs to prevent regressions
- Test user interactions and business logic, not implementation details
- Focus on behavior over internal state
- Implement tests at appropriate levels (unit, integration, e2e)

## Test Organization

- Keep tests close to the code they test
- Use descriptive test names that explain the scenario
- Group related tests using describe blocks
- Follow the AAA pattern: Arrange, Act, Assert

## React Component Testing

- Use React Testing Library for component tests
- Test component behavior from user perspective
- Mock external dependencies appropriately
- Test error boundaries and edge cases
- Avoid testing internal component state directly

## API and Business Logic Testing

- Test pure functions with comprehensive input/output scenarios
- Mock external API calls and services
- Test error handling and edge cases
- Validate data transformations and calculations
- Test async operations with proper awaiting

## Test Quality

- Keep tests simple, readable, and maintainable
- Use proper setup and teardown for test isolation
- Implement meaningful assertions with clear error messages
- Avoid flaky tests with proper synchronization
- Maintain test coverage for critical code paths

## Mocking Strategy

- Mock at the boundary of your system (APIs, databases)
- Use realistic test data that matches production scenarios
- Avoid over-mocking internal functions
- Mock time-dependent functionality for deterministic tests
- Reset mocks between test runs
